Fix Vulkan compute bindings and depth-byte re-encoding.

Compute helpers use explicit Vulkan bindings. The graphics register shifts
moved the depth shader's source image from binding 0 to binding 16 while its
descriptor layout still bound 0. Leave compute bindings unchanged.

Mask the high depth byte just as the CPU guest-memory conversion's u8 cast
does. At depth 1.0 the rounded float can become 0x1000000; an unmasked UNORM
store clamped its high byte to 255 where the CPU path stored zero.

Order each reuse of the shared depth-snapshot transfer buffer after the
previous snapshot's read. Multiple snapshots can share a command batch.

The GPU re-encoding path remains opt-in pending native visual comparison.

